# This is a sample survey description file.
#
# All lines starting with '#' are ignored, so they are used for comments
#
# Each data record can have any of the following formats.
# - it can be on 1 single line of format:
# [rect] <width> <height> <RA> <DEC> <epoch> <filling_factor> \
#   <obs_code> <efficiency_file_name>
#
# [rect]: optional, indicates this is a rectangular field
# <width>: width of FOV, in degree
# <height>: height of FOV, in degree
#
# - or on a signle line of format:
# ears <RA> <DEC> <epoch> <filling_factor> \
#   <obs_code> <efficiency_file_name>
#
# ears: indicates that the fields of view is a CFHT FoV, with the full 40-CCD
#       camera with side extensions
#
# - or it can be spread over N+1 lines of format:
# poly <N> <RA> <DEC> <epoch> <filling_factor> \
#   <obs_code> <efficiency_file_name>
# followed by N lines of format:
# <rel_ra> <rel_dec>
#
# poly: means we are giving the vertices of a polygon of N sides, as offsets
#       with respect to <RA>, <DEC>
# <N>: number of vertices or sides of the polygon
# <rel_ra>: longitude offset of the vertex with respect to <RA>
# <rel_dec>: latitude offset of the vertex with respect to <DEC>
#
# And the common parameters are:
#
# <RA>: Right Ascension of pointing, decimal degree or HH:MM:SS[.ss...]
# <DEC>: Declination of pointing, decimal degree or DD:MM:SS[.ss...]
# <epoch>: epoch of pointing, in Julian day (decimal)
# <filling_factor>: filling factor of that FOV
# <obs_code>: observatory code, or name of a CSV file
# <efficiency_file_name>: name of efficiency file for that pointing
#
# Only one block in the HST search
#
0.11 0.17 14:07:53.33 -11:21:38.0 2452667.9305555 1 HST.csv HST.eff
